*RECOVERY*.md
*recovery*.rs
memory_analysis.md
efr32-unlock/
xiao_mg24_flash_erase*/
*.zip

# Temporary documentation (not for repository)
docs/COMPREHENSIVE_FLASHING_GUIDE.md
docs/FLASHING_RESEARCH.md
docs/HOW_CLOCK_CONFIG_DISABLED_SWD.md
docs/PROBE_RS_EFR32MG24_ISSUES.md
docs/SAMD11_BRIDGE_AND_SAFE_FLASHING.md

# Archive backups (local only)
.archive/

# Cargo config overrides (local development)
.cargo/
efr32mg24-hal/examples/02_blink.rs

# Book writing (documentation project, not code)
book/output/
book/project/*/target/
*.pdf
# ...except the book itself, which is delivered as a reading copy at the root of the repository. Build output
# stays ignored; this one file is the product.
!Rust-Embedded-Hardware-Support.pdf
book/**/*.aux
book/**/*.log
book/**/*.out
book/**/*.toc

# Radio -sys crates: blobs and vendor headers (MSLA licensed, not in git)
**/blobs/*.a
**/blobs/*.o
**/blobs/*.lib
**/vendor/**/*.h
**/vendor/**/*.c
# ...except the vendor trees the build genuinely needs. The repository already ships the Silabs binaries these
# headers describe (the controller, host and NVM3 archives) and the whole v4.4.5 emlib source, so withholding the
# headers left a clone that could not build its own radio or BSP crates -- a repository that compiles only on the
# machine where the SDK happens to be unpacked.
!crates/efr32mg24-emlib-sys/vendor/**
!crates/efr32mg24-bluetooth-sys/vendor/**
!crates/efr32mg24-rail-sys/vendor/**

# Local temp work must not land in the repository
_tmp/

# Build artefacts and vendor packs never belong in the repository
*.hex
*.bin
*.pack
!scripts/**/*.hex

# Reverse-engineering tooling: the container recipe is a bench tool, not part of the crate
# (and the images it builds are large).
docker/
